<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibo Island</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibo is a small island of the Quirimbas archipelago off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-delgado">Cabo Delgado</a> province in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozambique">Mozambique</a>. Settled by the Portuguese, it became a fortified town in the late 18th century, the capital of the Cabo Delgado district and a centre of the slave and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> trade. It was the first headquarters of the Niassa Company before the move to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pemba-mozambique">Porto Amélia</a>, now Pemba, and its old town is a candidate World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ibo-island.jpg" alt="Ibo Island" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rosino · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ilha_do_Ibo-sunset-02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
